pictures on there already.


00:15:11.278 --> 00:15:15.046
[ Groans ]
Come on, Austin. Don't be
such a pain in the ass.


00:15:15.048 --> 00:15:16.214
Just do it--
for me.


00:15:16.216 --> 00:15:20.718
Oh. And, hon,
could you set up the camera
at the end of the car?


00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:23.421
Alisa and I
will be right back.


00:15:23.423 --> 00:15:25.556
Yeah?


00:15:29.128 --> 00:15:31.229
Bobby.
Bobby.


00:15:34.433 --> 00:15:36.668
[ Chattering ]


00:15:47.746 --> 00:15:50.248
[ Chattering Continues ]


00:15:51.583 --> 00:15:53.651
Oh!
[ Wolf Whistle ]


00:15:57.189 --> 00:15:58.189
Whoo!


00:15:58.191 --> 00:16:00.458
Now that is unbelievably hot.


00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:01.826
Like our new uniforms?


00:16:01.828 --> 00:16:03.561
- I love 'em, baby.
- [ Austin ]
This is ridiculous.


00:16:03.563 --> 00:16:09.200
We're supposed to be
running a racing team, not
selling tuner girl calendars.


00:16:09.202 --> 00:16:10.501
You know you're an ass,
right?


00:16:10.503 --> 00:16:15.606
Okay. Let's just line up
in front of the car,
take a picture.


00:16:15.608 --> 00:16:18.810
The fans are gonna
want to see us
before we leave for the race.


00:16:18.812 --> 00:16:22.547
- All right. Come on.
- Okay! Here's to
the Road Rally 1000!


00:16:22.549 --> 00:16:25.516
Here's to
the 100 grand purse!
Yeah!


00:16:25.518 --> 00:16:26.517
Whoo!


00:16:26.519 --> 00:16:30.621
- [ Flies Buzzing ]
- [ Camera Shutter Clicking ]


00:16:30.623 --> 00:16:32.423
<i>[ Police Radio Chatter ]</i>


00:16:32.425 --> 00:16:35.393
Hey, you the new guy?


00:16:35.395 --> 00:16:38.062
Yeah. Afternoon.


00:16:38.263 --> 00:16:40.398
You ever seen
anything like this before?


00:16:40.400 --> 00:16:42.467
Third body
in the last two months.


00:16:42.469 --> 00:16:44.736
- Jesus Christ. Really?
- Highway 17.


00:16:44.738 --> 00:16:47.138
They don't call it
Slaughter Alley for nothing.


00:16:47.140 --> 00:16:49.607
I don't follow.
[ Man ]
What do we got?


00:16:49.609 --> 00:16:52.844
Long-haul trucker
called it in.


00:16:52.846 --> 00:16:55.680
Body... parts.


00:16:55.682 --> 00:16:59.117
Two victims.
White male, female.


00:16:59.119 --> 00:17:00.351
No identification.


00:17:00.353 --> 00:17:03.521
We're still looking
for most of them.


00:17:03.523 --> 00:17:05.523
Hey. What caused this?


00:17:05.525 --> 00:17:09.260
It's hard to say really.
Well, it could have
been a murder.


00:17:13.832 --> 00:17:15.333
We'll know more once
we get all the body parts.


00:17:15.335 --> 00:17:18.770
And I'll let you know when
the medical examiner has done
his preliminary examination.


00:17:18.772 --> 00:17:21.539
Any hunch as to what might have
ripped them up like this?


00:17:21.541 --> 00:17:24.308
Could have been coyotes.
Could have been wolves.


00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:28.813
I mean,
they could have spread
the body parts all around.


00:17:28.815 --> 00:17:30.848
Okay.
Keep me informed.


00:17:30.850 --> 00:17:33.351
Yeah. Will do.


00:17:33.353 --> 00:17:35.319
[ Sighs ]
Sir.


00:17:35.321 --> 00:17:37.455
What do you want me
to write it up as?


00:17:37.457 --> 00:17:39.657
Write it up
as a possible
animal attack.


00:17:39.659 --> 00:17:42.760
It did look like they got
dragged. There's a lot of
road rash on those bodies.


00:17:42.762 --> 00:17:46.831
Do you think it's maybe
a good idea if I check around,
see if anybody heard anything?


00:17:46.833 --> 00:17:50.635
Check around
as much as you like.
Just don't start scaring people.


00:17:50.637 --> 00:17:56.274
We've got enough trouble
with this...
Slaughter Alley bullshit.


00:17:57.376 --> 00:17:59.343
I get it.
I'll keep it low-key.


00:17:59.345 --> 00:18:03.347
Radio me when you're
all cleaned up here.


00:18:04.383 --> 00:18:05.249
Will do.


00:18:05.251 --> 00:18:08.686
<i>[ Police Radio Chatter ]</i>
<i>[ Flies Buzzing ]</i>


00:18:08.688 --> 00:18:11.255
[ Engine Revving ]


00:18:11.824 --> 00:18:12.623
And?


00:18:12.625 --> 00:18:15.693
Slightly better
than the last run,
a three percent increase.


00:18:15.695 --> 00:18:16.794
Damn it.
I was kind of
hoping for more.


00:18:16.796 --> 00:18:20.865
Yeah, well, all this testing
really doesn't mean much.
We need a real-world dry run.


00:18:20.867 --> 00:18:23.534
Yeah, I know.
We just don't have the time.


00:18:23.536 --> 00:18:25.403
Well, we need to make the time.


00:18:25.405 --> 00:18:27.839
It's just stupid not
working out the engine.


00:18:27.841 --> 00:18:30.575
You calling me stupid?


00:18:30.843 --> 00:18:32.643
Yeah. Yeah, I am.
Yeah, you would.


00:18:32.645 --> 00:18:35.580
Besides, you know,
you should really
let me drive.


00:18:35.582 --> 00:18:37.248
I should let you drive,
shouldn't I?


00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:41.819
Okay. You know what?
I'll tell you what, big guy.
You can drive right now.


00:18:45.691 --> 00:18:48.860
- There you go.
You wanna drive?
- No, thanks.


00:18:48.862 --> 00:18:51.796
You sure?
Yeah, I'm sure.
You wanna get back in here?


00:18:51.798 --> 00:18:55.867
All right. Sit down back there.
You're making Bobby nervous.


00:18:55.869 --> 00:18:59.737
[ Chuckles ]
Whoo!


00:19:00.439 --> 00:19:02.640
What's that?


00:19:04.710 --> 00:19:06.777
<i>Relax, Mick.</i>
<i>All right. Who's hungry?</i>


00:19:06.779 --> 00:19:10.848
<i>Oh, yeah.</i>
<i>Good. There's a truck stop</i>
<i>two miles up with a café.</i>


00:19:10.850 --> 00:19:14.385
American fine dining
at its best.
Mmm, mmm, mmm, mmm.


00:19:14.387 --> 00:19:17.288
We're pulling over for lunch.


00:19:29.735 --> 00:19:33.204
[ Jewel ]
Is that a serious question?
Of course I do.


00:19:33.206 --> 00:19:35.573
[ Jordan ]
Just joking.


00:19:38.277 --> 00:19:40.178
Morning.


00:19:40.946 --> 00:19:45.183
Uh, excuse me.
I don't drink coffee.


00:19:51.557 --> 00:19:53.991
I'll be back for your order.


00:19:53.993 --> 00:19:56.327
Uh--


00:19:56.329 --> 00:19:58.629
Colorful.
Wow.


00:19:58.631 --> 00:19:59.463
Oh, my God.


00:19:59.465 --> 00:20:02.767
She's the spitting image
of Large Marge!


00:20:03.335 --> 00:20:06.404
- Who?
- Really?


00:20:06.605 --> 00:20:09.507
Anyone?
Large Marge?


00:20:09.875 --> 00:20:12.310
<i>Pee-wee's Big Adventure.</i>


00:20:12.312 --> 00:20:14.745
What are you
talking about, Bobby?


00:20:15.347 --> 00:20:19.083
You know, the youth today--
they've got no sense of history,
no sense of culture.


00:20:19.085 --> 00:20:22.987
- It's just devastating.
- [ Jewel ]
I'm sorry.


00:20:23.889 --> 00:20:26.657
[ Sighs ]
Move over.


00:20:26.792 --> 00:20:28.793
What are we talking about?


00:20:28.795 --> 00:20:30.795
Nothing.
Trust me.


00:20:31.897 --> 00:20:36.467
All right. Did you see
this route on your G.P.S.?


00:20:36.469 --> 00:20:38.903
No. Maybe it's an old route
they shut down.


00:20:38.905 --> 00:20:42.506
Okay, well, if it's open,
it'll be a more direct route.


00:20:42.508 --> 00:20:44.375
We could shave
a day off our time.


00:20:44.377 --> 00:20:49.280
Yeah, but if it's not
on the G.P.S., then it might
not even exist anymore.


00:20:49.282 --> 00:20:50.915
Right.


00:20:51.717 --> 00:20:53.951
So, what'll it be?


00:20:57.322 --> 00:20:58.389
Uh--
Burgers?


00:20:58.391 --> 00:20:59.490
- Burgers.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.


00:20:59.492 --> 00:21:01.525
Yeah. Burgers. Yeah.
Please. All around.


00:21:01.527 --> 00:21:04.929
Um, everything on them.
And we'll have 'em
to go, please.


00:21:04.931 --> 00:21:07.798
We're in a bit of a rush.


00:21:07.800 --> 00:21:10.034
Of course you are.


00:21:10.036 --> 00:21:11.736
Hmm.


00:21:11.738 --> 00:21:15.072
Thanks, Marge.
[ Both Laugh ]


00:21:15.074 --> 00:21:16.741
So what do you guys
want to do?


00:21:16.743 --> 00:21:20.845
I mean, I would love
an extra day on the course,
get the lay of the land.


00:21:20.847 --> 00:21:24.749
You're sitting
in a truck stop.
Ask a trucker. They'll know.


00:21:24.751 --> 00:21:27.585
Yeah, that's a good idea.


00:21:27.587 --> 00:21:29.553
Come on.


00:21:31.723 --> 00:21:33.891
Which one?


00:21:36.795 --> 00:21:38.362
Excuse me, sir.
Hi.


00:21:38.364 --> 00:21:40.731
Could we have
a moment of your time?
What do you want?


00:21:40.733 --> 00:21:44.402
Directions, actually.
Can I show you this map?


00:21:44.404 --> 00:21:46.504
Suit yourself.


00:21:47.939 --> 00:21:50.441
You recognize this highway?


00:21:50.443 --> 00:21:51.942
Route 17.


00:21:51.944 --> 00:21:56.047
Does it still exist?
'Cause we can't
find it on our G.P.S.


00:21:56.049 --> 00:21:58.916
It exists,
but you don't want to take it.


00:21:58.918 --> 00:22:00.918
Uh, why not?
We're heading up to Canada,


00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:03.988
and we figure that route
would cut at least
a day off our trip.


00:22:03.990 --> 00:22:08.659
Trust me,
you don't want to take it.


00:22:10.028 --> 00:22:13.564
Why not, exactly?
Is it a rough road?


00:22:13.566 --> 00:22:14.899
Is it under repair?
What?


00:22:14.901 --> 00:22:17.668
- You know what they call
that stretch of highway?
- No.


00:22:17.670 --> 00:22:19.804
- Slaughter Alley.
You know why?
- Obviously not.


00:22:19.806 --> 00:22:24.875
Because more people die or
disappear on that road than any
other road in the United States.


00:22:27.612 --> 00:22:30.414
- Really?
- Some say it's the road itself
that's dangerous.


00:22:30.416 --> 00:22:36.053
Well, I'm a pretty good driver.
I'm not gonna crash,
if that's what you mean.


00:22:36.055 --> 00:22:38.989
Well, you might just disappear.


00:22:38.991 --> 00:22:40.157
They say...


00:22:40.159 --> 00:22:44.028
a trucker patrols
that highway
looking for people to kill.


00:22:44.030 --> 00:22:47.465
You do know
that most serial killers
are truck drivers, right?


00:22:47.467 --> 00:22:49.767
No, that's not true.


00:22:49.769 --> 00:22:50.868
Ask him.


00:22:50.870 --> 00:22:53.137
Barry here trying to
scare you off Highway 17?


00:22:53.139 --> 00:22:55.706
Yeah.
There's nothing wrong
with that highway.


00:22:55.708 --> 00:22:58.976
Barry here has a flair
for the dramatic.
Pay no attention to him.


00:22:58.978 --> 00:23:02.446
Then why don't you tell them
what you were doing up there
this morning, Chris?


00:23:02.448 --> 00:23:05.416
There was a fatality.
An accident.
We are investigating.


00:23:05.418 --> 00:23:09.887
Well, it looked like
a murder to me,
some kind of satanic sacrifice.


00:23:09.889 --> 00:23:13.691
Jesus, Barry.
You need to get
back on your meds.


00:23:13.693 --> 00:23:16.527
Just stay below
the speed limit.
You'll be fine.


00:23:16.529 --> 00:23:21.365
That is until
your car shuts off by itself.


00:23:22.768 --> 00:23:24.502
What do you mean
by that?


00:23:24.504 --> 00:23:27.138
There's some sort of
electronic dead zone out there.


00:23:27.140 --> 00:23:29.473
Sometimes
everything just shuts off.


00:23:29.475 --> 00:23:32.510
Your phones. Your C.B.s.
Your engines. Your lights.


00:23:32.512 --> 00:23:36.147
Some say it's aliens.
I say it's the government,
the damn N.S.A.


00:23:36.149 --> 00:23:41.085
They've got some sort of
top secret giant listening post
out there in the wasteland.


00:23:41.087 --> 00:23:44.588
Wow.
They don't want us
to find out about it.


00:23:47.959 --> 00:23:48.859
Okay.


00:23:48.861 --> 00:23:51.128
Thank you very much
for sharing with us...


00:23:51.130 --> 00:23:53.664
your conspiracies
of government
and aliens and--


00:23:53.666 --> 00:23:57.268
We'll let you
get back to your meal.
Thank you.


00:23:57.270 --> 00:23:58.936
Yeah.
The map.


00:23:58.938 --> 00:24:00.871
Oh.
Yeah.


00:24:00.873 --> 00:24:04.708
Of course, it's the drug runners
you really have to worry about.


00:24:04.710 --> 00:24:07.978
Now them boys--
Ooh, they are ruthless.


00:24:07.980 --> 00:24:10.581
Slaughter Alley's
just a straight shot...


00:24:10.583 --> 00:24:16.687
from them socialist
industrial pot farms
they got up in Canada.


00:24:16.689 --> 00:24:17.221
Eh?


00:24:17.223 --> 00:24:21.592
[ Chuckles ]
It's not very well patrolled.


00:24:21.594 --> 00:24:26.030
So you don't wanna
run into one of them.


00:24:26.032 --> 00:24:29.633
[ All Laughing ]


00:24:30.602 --> 00:24:32.770
[ Sighs ]
No.


00:24:32.772 --> 00:24:34.805
Y'all have a nice day now.


00:24:34.807 --> 00:24:38.209
- See you later.
- [ Jordan ]
Yeah, you too.


00:24:40.712 --> 00:24:41.846
Wow.
Whoa!


00:24:41.848 --> 00:24:44.081
- Okay.
- That's amazing.


00:24:44.083 --> 00:24:45.916
So?
Intense. Intense.


00:24:45.918 --> 00:24:47.751
Let's take a ride
on Slaughter Alley.


00:24:47.753 --> 00:24:49.220
I don't see
how we can't.
Let's do it.


00:24:49.222 --> 00:24:50.955
What about the drug thing?
That was kind of legitimate.


00:24:50.957 --> 00:24:54.725
Yeah, and he also
talked about aliens and secret
government military sites.


00:24:54.727 --> 00:24:58.229
Come on. The guy said that
nobody patrols it really.
We could take the car,


00:24:58.231 --> 00:24:59.997
test it out,
really open her up.


00:24:59.999 --> 00:25:02.900
It's not a bad idea.
Well, we would have
a story to tell.


00:25:02.902 --> 00:25:04.869
I don't know.
[ Alisa ]
Let's do it.


00:25:04.871 --> 00:25:06.837
- Yeah?
- [ All ]
Yeah!


00:25:06.839 --> 00:25:08.772
I get to drive though.
No, no.


00:25:08.774 --> 00:25:11.809
Hey. Why do you
always get to drive?


00:25:14.579 --> 00:25:17.114
- Got this?
- Yeah.


00:25:18.650 --> 00:25:20.951
[ Door Opens ]


00:25:27.158 --> 00:25:28.659
Marge!


00:25:28.661 --> 00:25:32.029
Bobby, what the hell?
Large Marge!


00:25:32.031 --> 00:25:35.032
<i>♪ [ Rock ]</i>


00:25:35.034 --> 00:25:37.935
[ Chattering ]


00:25:45.610 --> 00:25:48.279
<i>♪ [ Man Singing, Indistinct ]</i>


00:25:48.281 --> 00:25:50.581
Here we go. Here we go.


00:25:50.583 --> 00:25:52.917
Here we go.


00:26:00.191 --> 00:26:00.791
Whoo!


00:26:00.793 --> 00:26:04.028
All right, Mick.
We're gonna backtrack 20 miles,
warm it up.


00:26:04.030 --> 00:26:06.096
- We'll catch up.
- Copy that.


00:26:06.098 --> 00:26:09.099
Give me updates
through handheld, all right?
Will do.


00:26:09.101 --> 00:26:10.768
Don't let him
crash that thing.


00:26:10.770 --> 00:26:14.405
<i>[ Man ]</i>
<i>♪ All I gotta do</i>
<i>is flash my lights</i>


00:26:14.407 --> 00:26:17.808
<i>♪ 'Cause this is my city</i>


00:26:17.810 --> 00:26:21.211
<i>♪ Baby, this is my town</i>


00:26:21.213 --> 00:26:25.182
<i>♪ And this is my city</i>


00:26:25.184 --> 00:26:27.718
<i>♪ Baby, this is my town</i>


00:26:27.720 --> 00:26:32.156
<i>♪ Well, I hear you found</i>
<i>somebody that's been</i>
<i>treating you right</i>


00:26:32.158 --> 00:26:36.093
<i>♪ I know you're not</i>
<i>playing me for a fool</i>


00:26:36.095 --> 00:26:38.829
[ Engine Revving ]


00:27:06.091 --> 00:27:07.458
<i>♪ [ Rock ]</i>


00:27:07.460 --> 00:27:11.662
All right.
We better turn it around,
catch up to the others.


00:27:11.664 --> 00:27:13.030
Okay.


00:27:23.174 --> 00:27:25.776
- Oh, you're redlining.
- I'm shifting.


00:27:25.778 --> 00:27:29.380
I'm just saying
don't blow the engine
before we get there. That's all.


00:27:29.382 --> 00:27:31.015
I know the limits
of this car.


00:27:31.017 --> 00:27:35.285
I know exactly how much
it'll take, and I'm not timid
about pushing her.


00:27:35.287 --> 00:27:37.921
[ Laughs ]
You think Jordan's timid?


00:27:37.923 --> 00:27:40.224
Jordan's smart.
He usually crosses
the finish line.


00:27:40.226 --> 00:27:42.760
He doesn't crash and burn
like some douche bag I know.


00:27:42.762 --> 00:27:44.361
Hey, that wasn't my fault.
The head gasket blew.


00:27:44.363 --> 00:27:48.866
And then you ran
the fucking car into the wall,
you spastic shithead.


00:27:48.868 --> 00:27:52.036
Whoa! Whoa, baby.
Thanks.


00:27:52.038 --> 00:27:55.039
I can take care of myself.


00:27:55.041 --> 00:27:58.776
Maybe I should drive.
[ Chuckles ]


00:28:09.454 --> 00:28:12.389
[ Engine Revving ]


00:28:13.458 --> 00:28:15.926
♪ [ Humming ]


00:28:19.230 --> 00:28:22.166
- Whoa, you might want to
slow it down a bit, huh?
- What for?


00:28:22.168 --> 00:28:25.803
- Well, you don't need to
scare the poor guy.
- Fuck him.


00:28:25.805 --> 00:28:27.838
Watch this.


00:28:39.484 --> 00:28:41.819
[ Brakes Screech ]


00:28:42.987 --> 00:28:45.489
[ Horn Blares ]


00:28:45.491 --> 00:28:46.790
Dude!


00:28:46.792 --> 00:28:49.259
That's a really
shitty thing to do, man.


00:28:49.261 --> 00:28:51.795
I'm just waking him up.


00:28:58.870 --> 00:29:02.339
- [ Jordan ] You just can't
help yourself, can you?
- [ Austin ] What?


00:29:02.341 --> 00:29:05.042
[ Jordan ]
Screwing with people
for the hell of it.


00:29:05.044 --> 00:29:07.311
[ Austin ]
It's a gift.


00:29:07.313 --> 00:29:10.180
Look, just pull over,
all right? I got it.


00:29:10.182 --> 00:29:14.451
I thought I was driving.
Look, I said just pull over.
Okay? Thank you.


00:29:53.525 --> 00:29:56.393
Stop it, man.
I will kill you.


00:29:57.328 --> 00:29:59.296
[ Horn Honks ]


00:29:59.298 --> 00:30:00.497
Hey!


00:30:03.301 --> 00:30:07.304
What took you so long?
Austin was busy making friends
with the local truckers.


00:30:07.306 --> 00:30:08.405
What?
Never mind.


00:30:08.407 --> 00:30:10.307
- How'd she run?
- Smooth.
Did a ton and a half.


00:30:10.309 --> 00:30:14.578
- Didn't even break a sweat.
- Nice.
Diagnostics working okay?


00:30:14.580 --> 00:30:16.480
All green.


00:30:16.915 --> 00:30:18.348
You know, if the car
is running so smooth,


00:30:18.350 --> 00:30:21.985
maybe you should consider
giving your mechanic
a little raise.


00:30:21.987 --> 00:30:25.255
- [ Horn Blares ]
- What the hell?


00:30:25.257 --> 00:30:26.323
What is that?


00:30:26.325 --> 00:30:28.358
Jesus, what's
that guy's problem?


00:30:28.360 --> 00:30:29.426
It's that guy
Austin pissed off.


00:30:29.428 --> 00:30:33.363
- Did I mention that was
an asshole move, by the way?
- [ Horn Blares ]


00:30:35.600 --> 00:30:38.202
What the hell's
this guy doing?


00:30:38.204 --> 00:30:40.404
- He's gonna try and pass us.
- That's fine.


00:30:40.406 --> 00:30:43.540
I'm just gonna be cool
and let him pass.


00:30:54.085 --> 00:30:57.254
[ Horn Blares ]


00:30:57.555 --> 00:30:58.622
[ Brakes Screeching ]


00:30:58.624 --> 00:31:02.226
- Oh, what an asshole.
- <i>[ Mickey ]</i>
<i>That guy nearly hit you.</i>


00:31:02.228 --> 00:31:04.862
[ Jordan ]
I know. I know.


00:31:05.196 --> 00:31:09.399
- Now he's slowing down.
- <i>Let's blow by this jerk</i>
<i>and leave him in our dust.</i>


00:31:09.401 --> 00:31:12.169
Yeah, let's teach
this guy a lesson.


00:31:13.371 --> 00:31:15.339
This guy's
a bigger prick than me.


00:31:15.341 --> 00:31:19.209
<i>[ Mickey ]</i>
<i>This guy is totally</i>
<i>fucking with you.</i>


00:31:20.044 --> 00:31:23.380
- <i>[ Jordan ]</i>
<i>I'll go left. You go right.</i>
<i>-</i> <i>[ Mickey ] Got it.</i>


00:31:34.025 --> 00:31:39.129
Can't get around him.
Can you see anything over there?
No. You've got nothing here.


00:31:42.634 --> 00:31:45.702
- [ Jordan ] This guy's good.
- [ Mickey ]
No, he's fucking nuts!


00:31:45.704 --> 00:31:50.540
- I'll play possum on the right.
It'll give you a window.
- <i>[ Jordan ] Yeah, I got it.</i>


00:31:55.146 --> 00:31:58.081
Yeah, that's right, bitch!


00:31:59.984 --> 00:32:04.454
My turn. Let's see
how this guy likes
his blind spot.


00:32:04.756 --> 00:32:08.191
Go! Go!
See how this guy
likes his blind spot.


00:32:09.160 --> 00:32:10.127
Gun him.


00:32:10.129 --> 00:32:12.362
- Whoo!
- [ Horn Blares ]


00:32:12.364 --> 00:32:14.564
[ Laughs ]
Got it.


00:32:18.403 --> 00:32:21.238
- He's coming back.
- What's with this guy?


00:32:29.480 --> 00:32:32.349
Holy shit!
I got it. I got it.
Hold on!


00:32:34.986 --> 00:32:36.987
Son of a bitch!


00:32:36.989 --> 00:32:38.455
<i>[ Jordan ]</i>
<i>You guys okay?</i>


00:32:38.457 --> 00:32:41.124
He just tried to run us
off the road.


00:32:41.126 --> 00:32:42.693
Fuck!


00:32:42.695 --> 00:32:45.128
You all right?


00:32:50.435 --> 00:32:53.403
<i>[ Mickey ]</i>
<i>He's coming for you now.</i>


00:33:03.181 --> 00:33:05.115
[ Horn Blares ]


00:33:05.117 --> 00:33:07.250
Yeah!


00:33:10.955 --> 00:33:12.389
<i>[ Mickey ]</i>
<i>Move, Jordan. Move!</i>


00:33:12.391 --> 00:33:15.959
[ Jordan ]
Relax. He couldn't
touch me if he tried.


00:33:18.663 --> 00:33:20.731
- Shit!
- [ Both Scream ]


00:33:22.233 --> 00:33:24.101
[ Horn Blares ]


00:33:50.661 --> 00:33:53.196
- Did he hit them?
- No. They're fine.


00:33:53.198 --> 00:33:57.300
- We should stop.
- [ Jordan ]
Trucker's fine.


00:33:57.302 --> 00:33:59.369
We should call the cops!


00:33:59.371 --> 00:34:01.171
Look, they're fine.
We're fine. Okay?


00:34:01.173 --> 00:34:04.641
- If we get the cops involved,
that could cost us a day.
- Jordan!


00:34:04.643 --> 00:34:07.711
Look, it's not like
we're completely innocent
here, babe, all right?


00:34:07.713 --> 00:34:12.215
If I get a driving mark
on my record, it could
cost us the race.


00:34:12.217 --> 00:34:15.419
Jordan's right.
We've got a race to run.


00:35:06.504 --> 00:35:11.842
Maybe we should just tell them
that he ran us off the road.
We could call it in anonymously.


00:35:11.844 --> 00:35:13.477
It's the right thing to do.


00:35:13.479 --> 00:35:16.313
Listen, guys.
If somebody got hurt,
I would have stopped.


00:35:16.315 --> 00:35:18.582
But nobody did, okay?
We're all fine.


00:35:18.584 --> 00:35:20.517
Trucks jackknife
all the time.


00:35:20.519 --> 00:35:22.752
Okay? Just trust me on this.


00:35:22.754 --> 00:35:25.288
I know what I'm doing.


00:35:26.491 --> 00:35:29.092
<i>[ Frequency Tuning ]</i>


00:35:32.763 --> 00:35:33.930
One Racer.


00:35:33.932 --> 00:35:38.201
Come back, One Racer.
Are you out there?


00:35:38.203 --> 00:35:40.670
- Who is it?
- I don't know.


00:35:40.672 --> 00:35:41.671
Who is this?


00:35:41.673 --> 00:35:45.775
Is this One Racer
in the fancy race car?


00:35:46.644 --> 00:35:50.213
- Yes, it is.
- Well, this is Rusty Nail.


00:35:50.215 --> 00:35:51.715
<i>[ Jordan ]</i>
<i>Who are you?</i>


00:35:51.717 --> 00:35:54.985
I'm the trucker you just
ran off the road,


00:35:54.987 --> 00:35:57.387
<i>Jordan.</i>


00:36:00.725 --> 00:36:05.262
- And how do you know my name?
- Oh, I know your name, Jordan.


00:36:05.264 --> 00:36:06.663
I know your whole team.


00:36:06.665 --> 00:36:08.732
<i>[ Jordan ]</i>
<i>Yeah, what do you want?</i>


00:36:08.734 --> 00:36:12.836
You're gonna have to pay
for what you did.


00:36:12.838 --> 00:36:14.004
You will.


00:36:14.006 --> 00:36:19.009
<i>And F.Y.I.,</i>
<i>you're not gonna</i>
<i>make it to that race.</i>


00:36:19.011 --> 00:36:21.912
Just shut it off!
Don't talk to him anymore.


00:36:26.717 --> 00:36:30.287
- Well, what are we gonna do?
- I don't know.
We just keep going.


00:36:30.289 --> 00:36:32.689
Drive hard for the border.
Hopefully we don't
run into him again.


00:36:32.691 --> 00:36:37.327
- He sounded pissed.
- Yeah, well, good thing he's in
a big rig 50 miles behind us.


00:36:37.329 --> 00:36:40.697
- We'll open that gap up.
- [ Phone Rings ]


00:36:43.234 --> 00:36:45.035
Yeah.
<i>[ Mickey ]</i>
<i>What have we gotten into?</i>


00:36:45.037 --> 00:36:48.772
Look, just stick
on our tail, okay?
We're gonna head for the border.


00:36:48.774 --> 00:36:52.509
Stay together.
<i>What if he calls the cops?</i>


00:36:52.511 --> 00:36:55.245
Just drive.


00:37:07.858 --> 00:37:10.560
[ Dog Barking In Distance ]


00:37:17.335 --> 00:37:20.604
[ Dogs Barking In Distance ]


00:37:28.946 --> 00:37:31.781
This place
is a beauty, huh?


00:37:31.949 --> 00:37:35.685
Here. Pay with cash.
Leave no paper trail.


00:37:35.920 --> 00:37:37.687
We'll try to hurry up.
All right, babe?


00:37:37.689 --> 00:37:42.392
He rammed me and just knocked
the trailer right off the back.
I didn't see anything.


00:37:42.394 --> 00:37:44.027
What's wrong?
Why you so mad?


00:37:44.029 --> 00:37:47.964
Because he should have stopped
and called the cops.
Now we could all get in trouble.


00:37:47.966 --> 00:37:50.133
Can we really?
Yeah. It was
a dumb thing to do.


00:37:50.135 --> 00:37:53.370
I always thought
he'd do the right thing,
but I guess I was wrong.


00:37:53.372 --> 00:37:56.473
<i>♪ [ Speakers: Country ]</i>


00:37:58.743 --> 00:37:59.709
Hello?


00:37:59.711 --> 00:38:01.077
What if he reported us,
Jordan?


00:38:01.079 --> 00:38:04.547
Well, if he saw
our license plate, there
could be a BOLO out for us.


00:38:04.549 --> 00:38:06.883
We have two cars.
We filled them up.


00:38:06.885 --> 00:38:08.918
Ah.


00:38:08.920 --> 00:38:11.688
You should have
let me fill you up.


00:38:12.923 --> 00:38:15.292
We got it.


00:38:15.793 --> 00:38:19.462
- What about your change?
- Keep it.


00:38:21.932 --> 00:38:22.632
[ Sniffs ]


00:38:22.634 --> 00:38:24.000
Whoa, whoa.
I can't get in any trouble.


00:38:24.002 --> 00:38:26.369
[ Mickey ]
You? You're not the one
with a criminal record, dipshit.


00:38:26.371 --> 00:38:28.905
Which is why
we gotta get to the border--
to avoid the police.


00:38:28.907 --> 00:38:31.608
You know what?
You're making
the wrong decision.


00:38:31.610 --> 00:38:35.845
You're being a fucking idiot.
You can't make that decision
for the rest of us.


00:38:35.847 --> 00:38:38.114
- I know what I'm doing,
Jewel.
- Yeah! You keep saying that.


00:38:38.116 --> 00:38:40.450
But the truth is
you don't know
what you're doing,


00:38:40.452 --> 00:38:42.552
and you're not gonna be
doing it anymore.


00:38:42.554 --> 00:38:46.423
Austin, you started this shit.
We're gonna take the support
truck to the next town,


00:38:46.425 --> 00:38:49.392
and we're going to the police.
That is that.


00:38:49.394 --> 00:38:50.427
Come on.


00:38:50.429 --> 00:38:51.661
Yeah,
and what about the race?


00:38:51.663 --> 00:38:56.700
You know what, Jordan?
Go to the race.
Do what you want. I don't care.


00:38:56.702 --> 00:38:59.069
I'm doing this.


00:39:24.962 --> 00:39:27.931
<i>[ C.B. Radio Chatter ]</i>


00:39:30.067 --> 00:39:32.635
Well, it doesn't
sound like the police
are looking for us.


00:39:32.637 --> 00:39:35.705
For now.
No, no, no. They repeat
BOLOs all the time.


00:39:35.707 --> 00:39:39.576
There's been nothing
but the usual chatter
for the last hour or so.


00:39:39.578 --> 00:39:42.779
- Still doesn't mean anything.
- [ Loud Pop ]


00:39:42.781 --> 00:39:44.881
Jesus!


00:39:49.186 --> 00:39:51.755
[ Engine Stops ]
[ Sighs ]


00:39:52.490 --> 00:39:56.693
- You're changing the tire.
- Gee, thanks.


00:40:02.500 --> 00:40:04.100
Oh.


00:40:04.568 --> 00:40:06.469
[ Jewel Groans ]


00:40:13.110 --> 00:40:14.878
Oh. That's weird.


00:40:14.880 --> 00:40:16.813
G.P.S. cut out,
and it's on satellite.


00:40:16.815 --> 00:40:21.818
Let me check the G.P.S. app
on my phone.


00:40:21.820 --> 00:40:23.620
No bars.


00:40:24.021 --> 00:40:27.590
Well, I guess
we keep driving
till we hit a cell tower.


00:40:27.592 --> 00:40:31.861
Make yourself useful,
and put this away.


00:40:38.135 --> 00:40:40.503
[ Jewel Sighs ]


00:40:41.539 --> 00:40:45.108
- What are you doing?
- Driving.


00:40:46.844 --> 00:40:49.446
[ Engine Starts ]


00:40:52.016 --> 00:40:54.784
[ Austin ]
How far ahead do you think
Jordan and the others are?


00:40:54.786 --> 00:40:57.821
We broke down for, what,
30 minutes?
Yeah, about that.


00:40:57.823 --> 00:41:01.124
They could be as far
as 45 miles ahead.


00:41:01.126 --> 00:41:04.060
Oh. Still no cell service.


00:41:04.829 --> 00:41:07.063
Try the C.B.?


00:41:10.267 --> 00:41:12.168
Testing.


00:41:14.638 --> 00:41:17.507
Hello. Is anybody out there?
Testing!


00:41:17.641 --> 00:41:22.045
<i>[ Static Clicks ]</i>
<i>Hey. It's working.</i>


00:41:22.047 --> 00:41:24.581
[ Horn Blares ]


00:41:24.583 --> 00:41:26.082
Shit!


00:41:27.852 --> 00:41:30.453
What the fuck is that?


00:41:31.055 --> 00:41:34.491
- Shit.
- Just-- Just speed up.


00:41:35.960 --> 00:41:38.795
This guy's a fucking psycho.
Why is he doing this to us?


00:41:38.797 --> 00:41:40.930
I don't know!
Just keep going.


00:41:42.933 --> 00:41:44.734
[ Screams ]


00:41:44.736 --> 00:41:46.703
Austin, do something!


00:41:48.038 --> 00:41:50.073
Oh, God.


00:41:51.809 --> 00:41:53.376
- Call for help!
- Jordan!


00:41:53.378 --> 00:41:58.047
- Call for help! Come on!
- Jordan! It's Austin.
Come in!


00:42:02.086 --> 00:42:05.889
- Oh, my God!
- Jordan, come in!
It's Austin.


00:42:05.891 --> 00:42:08.124
Got any signal yet?


00:42:09.660 --> 00:42:11.794
[ Sighs ]


00:42:13.330 --> 00:42:15.698
No. There's nothing.


00:42:19.036 --> 00:42:20.904
My God!


00:42:22.907 --> 00:42:25.975
He's coming alongside of us.


00:42:28.045 --> 00:42:31.714
He's gonna pass us.
Oh, my God.
What do I do?


00:42:34.018 --> 00:42:36.686
What do I do?


00:42:48.966 --> 00:42:50.833
[ Shouting ]


00:43:08.085 --> 00:43:11.854
[ Reverse Indicator Beeping ]


00:43:21.332 --> 00:43:22.699
<i>[ Static Clicks ]</i>


00:43:22.701 --> 00:43:24.634
- There. I got it.
- Really?


00:43:24.636 --> 00:43:26.636
Yeah.
Well, call them up.


00:43:27.972 --> 00:43:31.307
<i>Austin, Jewel, come in.</i>


00:43:32.743 --> 00:43:35.311
Austin, Jewel, come in.
Over.


00:43:37.948 --> 00:43:40.850
Austin, come in, buddy.
It's Mickey.


00:43:43.120 --> 00:43:46.789
I got a signal.
I'll try giving Jewel a call.


00:43:47.725 --> 00:43:51.694
Austin. Come on, buddy.
We really need to hear from you.


00:43:57.067 --> 00:44:01.704
<i>[ Jewel On Recording ]</i>
<i>Hi. It's Jewel.</i>
<i>You know what to do.</i>


00:44:01.706 --> 00:44:02.405
Voice mail.


00:44:02.407 --> 00:44:08.778
Well, they're probably just
going through the same stretch
of road we just went through.


00:44:08.780 --> 00:44:10.146
Yeah.


00:44:29.767 --> 00:44:32.035
[ Chuckles ]


00:44:35.272 --> 00:44:37.306
Please.


00:44:37.308 --> 00:44:40.376
Why are you doing this?


00:44:41.311 --> 00:44:43.680
Just leave us alone.


00:44:50.988 --> 00:44:52.722
Please.


00:44:52.724 --> 00:44:53.756
Listen to me.


00:44:53.758 --> 00:44:58.494
Look, I didn't mean it, man.
We were just kidding around.


00:44:58.496 --> 00:45:00.163
Please!


00:45:00.364 --> 00:45:03.066
Where are you taking me, man?
No, please!


00:45:03.068 --> 00:45:05.201
- Keep walking.
- Please.


00:45:05.203 --> 00:45:08.771
- Here we go.
- No, no, no, no, no, no, no.


00:45:10.140 --> 00:45:14.744
Are you a religious man,
Austin?


00:45:14.746 --> 00:45:16.813
No! No. I mean, yes.
I mean, I--


00:45:16.815 --> 00:45:20.183
Look, I can be.
I will be from now on.
No, no. Please!


00:45:20.185 --> 00:45:22.385
Please! I'll do anything!


00:45:23.087 --> 00:45:25.988
- No!
- What is it they say?


00:45:26.256 --> 00:45:30.526
Idle hands
are the devil's workshop.


00:45:30.528 --> 00:45:32.462
- No!
- [ Laughing ]


00:45:32.464 --> 00:45:34.397
No, no, no, no, no!


00:45:34.399 --> 00:45:36.399
No, no, no, no!


00:45:36.401 --> 00:45:39.769
[ Screams ]


00:45:47.978 --> 00:45:50.413
I think I prefer
the one that says...


00:45:50.415 --> 00:45:56.219
if your hand causes you
to stumble, cut it off.


00:45:57.821 --> 00:46:00.156
No, no, no, no. No!


00:46:00.158 --> 00:46:02.425
No, no, no, no.


00:46:02.427 --> 00:46:05.862
[ Screaming ]


00:46:17.341 --> 00:46:23.212
Or maybe I'll just
go for the one that says...


00:46:23.214 --> 00:46:25.281
an eye for an eye.


00:46:25.283 --> 00:46:27.917
[ Screaming ]


00:46:53.410 --> 00:46:55.111
I'm getting worried.


00:46:55.113 --> 00:46:58.347
- I know.
- I think we should
turn around.


00:46:58.582 --> 00:47:01.484
Yeah. She's right, Jordan.
We need to see if they're okay.


00:47:01.486 --> 00:47:04.120
They could--
They could be broken down.


00:47:04.122 --> 00:47:06.522
Or in jail.


00:47:06.924 --> 00:47:09.358
Look, we've got
cell phone and C.B.
reception for now,


00:47:09.360 --> 00:47:13.963
so if we don't hear from them
in 15 minutes, we turn around.


00:47:13.965 --> 00:47:14.897
Fine.
Okay.


00:47:14.899 --> 00:47:18.501
Fair enough.
You got 15 minutes
starting now.


00:47:26.643 --> 00:47:29.111
[ Beeps ]


00:47:36.086 --> 00:47:39.822
It's time we had
a little chat.


00:47:54.504 --> 00:47:57.373
<i>[ Radio Static ]</i>
<i>[ Rusty ]</i>
<i>One Racer.</i>


00:47:57.375 --> 00:47:59.742
<i>One Racer.</i>
<i>Come in, Jordan.</i>


00:47:59.744 --> 00:48:03.112
<i>It's your pal,</i>
<i>Rusty Nail.</i>


00:48:03.114 --> 00:48:04.881
Pal.


00:48:05.315 --> 00:48:09.085
- Yeah, what do you want?
- Oh, it's not what I want.


00:48:09.087 --> 00:48:11.554
It's what I have
that <i>you</i> want.


00:48:12.522 --> 00:48:13.522
Yeah?
What's that?


00:48:13.524 --> 00:48:19.528
Your pretty little girlfriend
and your cocky co-driver.


00:48:19.530 --> 00:48:22.298
Yeah, how do I know
you have them?


00:48:23.367 --> 00:48:25.167
[ Grunts ]
Jordan, please.


00:48:25.169 --> 00:48:27.970
- Come get me, please!
- Fuck!


00:48:28.972 --> 00:48:32.141
<i>[ Rusty ]</i>
<i>Believe me now?</i>


00:48:32.143 --> 00:48:33.109
Oh--


00:48:33.111 --> 00:48:34.944
Look, just please
don't hurt them, okay?


00:48:34.946 --> 00:48:36.612
Please.
It was an accident.


00:48:36.614 --> 00:48:38.447
Oh, no, no, no.


00:48:38.449 --> 00:48:41.417
Sorry. No deal.
You're gonna have to pay.


00:48:41.419 --> 00:48:43.419
Yeah, how much?
I'll pay whatever you want.


00:48:43.421 --> 00:48:47.089
I don't think pocket change
is gonna cover it, Jordan.


00:48:47.091 --> 00:48:50.059
But, uh, there is a way
you could make me whole.


00:48:50.061 --> 00:48:52.662
- How?
- <i>That fancy race car of yours.</i>


00:48:52.664 --> 00:48:55.998
- I'll trade you
Austin and Jewel for the car.
- You gotta do it.


00:48:56.000 --> 00:48:57.233
- That should make us even.
- Fuck it.


00:48:57.235 --> 00:49:00.202
Yeah, deal. Done.
Just don't hurt them,
okay? Please.


00:49:00.204 --> 00:49:04.707
There's, uh, an old warehouse
off Highway 17...


00:49:04.709 --> 00:49:06.275
<i>on Four Points Road.</i>


00:49:06.277 --> 00:49:09.578
One hour, or you will never
see your friends again.


00:49:09.580 --> 00:49:11.347
How far?
No, there's no way.


00:49:11.349 --> 00:49:14.016
What do you mean?
It's almost a hundred miles.


00:49:14.018 --> 00:49:15.685
There's no way
we're gonna make it.


00:49:15.687 --> 00:49:17.787
Look, we need more time.


00:49:17.789 --> 00:49:21.123
Look, can you hear me?
We need more time
to get there. Come on.


00:49:21.125 --> 00:49:22.391
We gotta go.
Are you there?


00:49:22.393 --> 00:49:25.594
- We gotta go! Let's go!
- [ Tires Squealing ]


00:49:33.170 --> 00:49:34.503
[ Moans, Sobs ]


00:49:34.505 --> 00:49:37.740
Say cheese.
Just one for the record.


00:49:37.742 --> 00:49:42.378
- [ Shutter Clicks ]
- [ Siren Wails, Stops ]


00:50:13.443 --> 00:50:15.044
This is Williams.


00:50:15.046 --> 00:50:17.680
I got a crashed truck
on Route 17.


00:50:17.682 --> 00:50:20.616
I need an ambulance
and a wrecker. Over.


00:50:20.618 --> 00:50:22.718
<i>[ Man ]</i>
<i>Roger that.</i>


00:50:23.420 --> 00:50:25.388
- Jenkins, you there?
- <i>Yeah.</i>


00:50:25.390 --> 00:50:26.655
<i>What's the situation?</i>


00:50:26.657 --> 00:50:29.291
You gotta get out here
and see this.


00:50:30.127 --> 00:50:32.161
[ Moans ]


00:50:32.163 --> 00:50:34.130
Wake up.


00:50:35.165 --> 00:50:37.400
[ Grunts ]
Wake up, Sleeping Beauty.


00:50:37.402 --> 00:50:41.737
[ Coughs ]
That was a nasty wreck.


00:50:41.739 --> 00:50:44.740
And that is a nasty gash.
[ Sobs ]


00:50:44.742 --> 00:50:49.445
Why don't you tell Jordan
where you need to go.


00:50:50.380 --> 00:50:53.249
Tell Jordan!
I need to go
to the hospital.


00:50:53.251 --> 00:50:55.317
Louder!
I need to go
to the hospital!


00:50:55.319 --> 00:51:00.456
And what does Jordan have to do
so you can go to the hospital?


00:51:00.458 --> 00:51:01.657
Give you the car!


00:51:01.659 --> 00:51:04.427
Give me what?
Give you the car.


00:51:04.429 --> 00:51:07.129
Very good.
Please don't do this.


00:51:07.131 --> 00:51:11.200
Untie me.
I don't want him to--


00:51:11.202 --> 00:51:14.770
[ Screams, Sobs ]


00:51:20.844 --> 00:51:22.778
We gotta have a plan.


00:51:22.780 --> 00:51:24.146
We give him the car.


00:51:24.148 --> 00:51:26.482
We get Austin and Jewel,
and we call the cops.


00:51:26.484 --> 00:51:29.318
We tell them he kidnapped
our friends and stole our car.


00:51:29.320 --> 00:51:30.719
What if he
double-crosses us?


00:51:30.721 --> 00:51:33.255
We can't take a chance
with their lives.


00:51:33.257 --> 00:51:34.423
Look, she's right.
We can't.


00:51:34.425 --> 00:51:36.659
I'm not saying
we take a chance
with their lives.


00:51:36.661 --> 00:51:39.228
All I'm saying is
I don't trust this fucker.


00:51:39.230 --> 00:51:42.465
Yeah?
What'd you have in mind?


00:52:18.368 --> 00:52:19.935
Jordan.


00:52:19.937 --> 00:52:21.770
All right,
I'm gonna walk in from here.


00:52:21.772 --> 00:52:25.174
You two go down the sides, okay?
Stay within eye contact.


00:52:25.176 --> 00:52:28.244
Stay hidden.
He can't see you, only me.


00:52:28.246 --> 00:52:29.411
All right.
Good luck.


00:52:29.413 --> 00:52:33.916
- Hey. Give me a second to get
in position, all right?
- Yeah.


00:52:33.918 --> 00:52:36.252
- Hey. I'm coming with you.
- No.


00:52:36.254 --> 00:52:37.653
What?
No. You're staying here.
It's too dangerous.


00:52:37.655 --> 00:52:40.723
Besides, someone's
gotta stay with the car
in case something happens.


00:52:40.725 --> 00:52:42.324
I'm not staying here.
Yes, you are.


00:52:42.326 --> 00:52:44.960
You stay in the car,
and you keep the doors locked.


00:52:44.962 --> 00:52:47.229
Let me handle this, okay?


00:52:47.231 --> 00:52:49.465
I'll come back for you.
Okay.


00:52:53.270 --> 00:52:55.504
- These are my keys.
- [ Keys Jingling ]


00:52:55.506 --> 00:52:59.275
This'll all be over
in a few minutes.
All right.


00:53:06.650 --> 00:53:10.286
<i>[ Wind Whistling ]</i>


00:53:21.364 --> 00:53:23.799
This is Jordan.
I'm here.


00:53:25.435 --> 00:53:29.572
I have the car,
and I want my friends back.


00:53:29.574 --> 00:53:31.607
Five minutes to spare.


00:53:31.609 --> 00:53:34.910
I'm ready for the exchange.
I have the keys.


00:53:34.912 --> 00:53:36.712
The car's at the entrance.


00:53:36.714 --> 00:53:39.915
Just come on in.
I'll tell you when to stop.


00:53:39.917 --> 00:53:43.586
Look, I wanna talk
to my friends to know
that they're all right.


00:53:43.588 --> 00:53:46.989
You are in no position
to be making demands.


00:53:46.991 --> 00:53:51.727
- I wanna talk to them!
- Fine.


00:53:51.729 --> 00:53:53.629
Check your phone.


00:53:57.701 --> 00:54:02.605
<i>...do so you can go</i>
<i>to the hospital?</i>
<i>Give you the car!</i>


00:54:02.607 --> 00:54:03.439
You fucker.


00:54:03.441 --> 00:54:07.376
<i>Give me what?</i>
<i>Give you the car.</i>


00:54:07.378 --> 00:54:08.911
<i>[ Sobbing ]</i>


00:54:08.913 --> 00:54:11.046
You better not have hurt her!


00:54:11.048 --> 00:54:15.818
You come in now...
or this is off.


00:54:59.929 --> 00:55:03.399
[ Wings Fluttering ]


00:57:10.794 --> 00:57:12.861
Look, I'm here.
I got the keys.


00:57:12.863 --> 00:57:15.464
Now bring me my friends.


00:57:16.199 --> 00:57:18.667
I'm standing
in front of your truck.


00:57:18.669 --> 00:57:23.739
Okay, I held up
my part of the deal.
Now you hold up yours.


00:57:28.511 --> 00:57:30.612
- Hey!
- [ Wings Fluttering ]


00:57:30.614 --> 00:57:32.614
I know you can hear me!


00:57:32.616 --> 00:57:35.050
Come out and talk to me!


00:57:39.923 --> 00:57:41.990
[ Whispering ]
Bobby?


00:57:43.159 --> 00:57:44.159
Hey!


00:57:44.161 --> 00:57:47.629
[ Footsteps ]


00:57:54.704 --> 00:57:55.838
[ Screams ]


00:57:55.840 --> 00:57:57.473
Alisa!


00:57:58.107 --> 00:57:59.107
Hey!


00:57:59.843 --> 00:58:03.011
[ Horn Blares ]


00:58:15.592 --> 00:58:18.160
[ Jordan ]
Let's go! Let's go!


00:58:20.096 --> 00:58:22.898
Move it! Move it!
[ Alisa ]
Hurry!


00:58:24.300 --> 00:58:25.234
Where's Bobby?
I don't know.


00:58:25.236 --> 00:58:28.570
[ Alisa ] I haven't seen him.
We gotta go.
We can't wait for him.


00:58:28.572 --> 00:58:30.239
We gotta move!


00:58:50.627 --> 00:58:52.160
What the hell?


00:58:52.162 --> 00:58:58.133
- [ Siren Wailing ]
- [ Truck Horn Blaring ]


01:00:19.916 --> 01:00:22.918
Step out
of the truck slowly.


01:00:23.720 --> 01:00:27.889
Get out of
the goddamn vehicle now!


01:00:32.795 --> 01:00:35.664
Slowly! Slowly!


01:00:35.898 --> 01:00:38.133
Hands where
I can see 'em!


01:00:39.135 --> 01:00:41.903
Hands up over your head!


01:00:41.905 --> 01:00:43.405
Higher!


01:00:43.407 --> 01:00:45.741
On your knees.


01:00:51.381 --> 01:00:53.749
Hands behind your head.


01:00:53.751 --> 01:00:56.985
Lock your
goddamn fingers, now!


01:00:58.788 --> 01:01:01.089
Don't you fucking move.


01:01:13.202 --> 01:01:14.369
Left or right?


01:01:14.371 --> 01:01:16.805
Fuck it.
I don't know.
Go right.


01:01:21.911 --> 01:01:23.011
Call the police.


01:01:23.013 --> 01:01:25.447
It's about time
you came to your senses.


01:01:25.449 --> 01:01:26.415
I'll call.


01:01:26.417 --> 01:01:28.950
What's in the truck?


01:01:30.787 --> 01:01:33.155
Oh. What's that
up ahead?


01:01:33.157 --> 01:01:35.257
Hey.
[ Mickey ]
What?


01:01:35.259 --> 01:01:37.826
Highway Patrol car.
Yes!


01:01:51.774 --> 01:01:54.142
[ Mickey ]
Hey! Hey!


01:01:54.144 --> 01:01:54.976
Hey!


01:01:54.978 --> 01:01:57.212
- [ Jordan ] Officer, help!
- Put your hands
above your heads!


01:01:57.214 --> 01:01:59.347
Put your hands
above your heads right now!


01:01:59.349 --> 01:02:01.983
[ Mickey ] Easy.
We got an emergency.
You need to listen to us.


01:02:01.985 --> 01:02:04.152
- [ Alisa ] Our friends
have been kidnapped.
- You have to help us.


01:02:04.154 --> 01:02:07.823
- Are you the kids
from the diner?
- Yeah, yeah, that's us.


01:02:14.363 --> 01:02:15.030
Fresh meat?


01:02:15.032 --> 01:02:19.034
Look, a trucker
kidnapped our friend, okay?
Can I show you something?


01:02:19.036 --> 01:02:23.939
- Don't fucking move!
- Whoa! Whoa!
It's a cell phone, dude.


01:02:23.941 --> 01:02:24.439
Slowly.


01:02:24.441 --> 01:02:28.777
Okay, I just wanna
show you something, okay?
It's a picture.


01:02:28.779 --> 01:02:31.847
All right?
It's just a picture.


01:02:31.849 --> 01:02:33.415
It's my girlfriend.


01:02:33.417 --> 01:02:34.950
He took her.


01:02:34.952 --> 01:02:38.120
Okay, you can put
your hands down now.


01:02:39.088 --> 01:02:41.256
Okay, tell me
what happened.


01:02:41.258 --> 01:02:43.058
This trucker,
he took two of our friends.


01:02:43.060 --> 01:02:45.026
We were gonna do
this exchange
at a warehouse.


01:02:45.028 --> 01:02:48.163
We met him.
We were gonna give him
the car for our friends.


01:02:48.165 --> 01:02:49.498
He tried to hit me
with his big rig.


01:02:49.500 --> 01:02:51.867
Okay? But we don't know
where the hell he went.


01:02:51.869 --> 01:02:53.468
Did you see a truck
go this way at all?


01:02:53.470 --> 01:02:56.004
Yeah.
About 15 minutes ago.


01:02:56.006 --> 01:02:57.305
- A black Peterbilt?
- Yeah, it was.


01:02:57.307 --> 01:02:59.574
- That's him.
- Okay, you kids
get back in the car.


01:02:59.576 --> 01:03:01.877
You follow me.
We'll catch him.


01:03:03.112 --> 01:03:06.581
I was deadheading
back from Fargo.
I get a call from dispatch.


01:03:06.583 --> 01:03:09.518
They've got a rush load.
The refrigeration unit is out.


01:03:09.520 --> 01:03:12.320
So I was trying to haul ass
to the processing plant...


01:03:12.322 --> 01:03:14.890
before the whole
damn load rotted.


01:03:22.298 --> 01:03:25.934
Jesus Christ!
What the fuck did you do?


01:03:25.936 --> 01:03:29.371
Get down on the ground!
Get down on your knees
right fucking now!


01:03:29.373 --> 01:03:30.572
Whoa! Whoa!
What did you do?


01:03:30.574 --> 01:03:32.440
I swear to God
I had nothing
to do with this.


01:03:32.442 --> 01:03:35.010
- On the fucking ground!
- I had nothing to do with this!


01:03:35.012 --> 01:03:36.244
I just picked up
a rogue load.


01:03:36.246 --> 01:03:38.480
Some guy on the C.B. called,
said his truck broke.


01:03:38.482 --> 01:03:42.784
Face down
on the fucking ground!
On the fucking ground now!


01:03:45.154 --> 01:03:47.556
Whoa. Whoa, whoa, whoa.
What is that?


01:03:49.458 --> 01:03:52.127
[ Mickey, Jordan ]
Oh, shit!


01:03:52.129 --> 01:03:53.829
[ All ]
Hey!


01:04:02.605 --> 01:04:05.006
Ohh!
Go! Follow him!


01:04:05.008 --> 01:04:06.908
Yeah, yeah, yeah!


01:04:07.543 --> 01:04:10.078
Jenkins, this is Williams.


01:04:10.080 --> 01:04:12.113
I got him.
I got our killer. Over.


01:04:12.115 --> 01:04:16.351
I swear to God.
I had nothing to fucking
do with this.


01:04:16.353 --> 01:04:18.620
Jenkins, this is Williams.


01:04:18.622 --> 01:04:21.156
I've got our suspect in custody.


01:04:21.158 --> 01:04:25.827
I repeat: I've got
our suspect in custody. Over.


01:04:28.698 --> 01:04:32.100
[ Rusty ]
One Racer.
Come back, One Racer.


01:04:32.602 --> 01:04:34.302
Yeah,
this is One Racer.


01:04:34.304 --> 01:04:36.137
You broke the rules,
Jordan.


01:04:36.139 --> 01:04:39.007
You killed a police officer.
<i>Yes, I did.</i>


01:04:39.009 --> 01:04:40.675
<i>Now one of you</i>
<i>is gonna have to pay...</i>


01:04:40.677 --> 01:04:42.544
<i>with a lot more</i>
<i>than just a fucking car.</i>


01:04:42.546 --> 01:04:46.081
I want you to listen
to what you've wrought.


01:04:46.083 --> 01:04:49.317
Dispatch, this is Williams.
Have you heard from Jenkins?


01:04:49.319 --> 01:04:52.687
<i>Not a peep, Charlie.</i>
<i>What's going on out there?</i>


01:04:52.689 --> 01:04:53.555
[ Softly ]
Damn it.


01:04:53.557 --> 01:04:57.926
I got a murder suspect.
I'm bringing him in
for questioning.


01:04:57.928 --> 01:05:00.295
Find Jenkins, now.


01:05:00.297 --> 01:05:03.331
[ Bobby ]
Help!


01:05:03.333 --> 01:05:05.967
Somebody, please!


01:05:05.969 --> 01:05:08.403
Help!


01:05:08.405 --> 01:05:11.106
[ Screaming ]


01:05:11.108 --> 01:05:15.577
[ Wheezes, Screams ]


01:05:15.579 --> 01:05:17.279
Please, somebody!


01:05:17.281 --> 01:05:19.147
[ Muffled ]
No!


01:05:19.149 --> 01:05:22.350
No! No!


01:05:22.352 --> 01:05:24.653
Oh, God, no!


01:05:24.655 --> 01:05:26.621
Oh, God, no!


01:05:26.623 --> 01:05:28.723
[ Muffled Screaming ]


01:05:28.725 --> 01:05:31.626
Oh, God!


01:05:31.628 --> 01:05:33.528
Oh, God!


01:05:42.338 --> 01:05:43.204
One Racer.


01:05:43.206 --> 01:05:47.509
- <i>Come back, One Racer.</i>
<i>- Yeah, this is Jordan.</i>


01:05:47.511 --> 01:05:49.210
Hello, Jordan.


01:05:49.212 --> 01:05:50.612
I want you
to listen and learn.


01:05:50.614 --> 01:05:54.015
<i>This is what happens</i>
<i>when you break the rules.</i>


01:05:54.017 --> 01:05:57.385
- Say hello, Bobby.
- Jordan, please help me!


01:05:57.387 --> 01:05:59.654
[ Sobs ]


01:06:00.156 --> 01:06:00.588
Shit.


01:06:00.590 --> 01:06:03.091
- [ Mickey ] Fuck.
- Don't you hurt him, okay?


01:06:03.093 --> 01:06:07.429
Way too late for that,
my friend.
No. No.


01:06:08.364 --> 01:06:12.701
- [ Screaming ]
- Fuck!


01:06:12.703 --> 01:06:15.036
Help me!
Fucking help me!


01:06:15.038 --> 01:06:17.339
[ Screaming ]


01:06:18.407 --> 01:06:22.210
- Jewel! Jewel!
- [ Flesh Squishing ]


01:06:22.212 --> 01:06:24.045
How does that feel
in there, Bobby?


01:06:24.047 --> 01:06:28.283
- [ Screaming ]
- Please make him stop.


01:06:28.285 --> 01:06:31.353
Getting a little snug,
I bet.


01:06:31.355 --> 01:06:33.722
<i>[ Chuckling ]</i>


01:06:44.200 --> 01:06:46.334
Please let him go!


01:06:50.106 --> 01:06:51.473
No! Please!


01:07:02.218 --> 01:07:04.219
Fuck!
[ Grunts ]


01:07:10.659 --> 01:07:12.394
Turn this thing off!


01:07:23.339 --> 01:07:24.706
[ Whirring, Hissing ]


01:07:24.708 --> 01:07:26.708
What the fuck was that?


01:07:26.710 --> 01:07:30.178
[ Whirring Stops ]


01:07:30.746 --> 01:07:32.347
<i>You caused this, Jordan.</i>


01:07:32.349 --> 01:07:36.351
<i>You made the choice,</i>
<i>and now your friend is dead.</i>


01:07:36.353 --> 01:07:37.052
<i>Can you live with that?</i>


01:07:37.054 --> 01:07:40.321
<i>Can you wake up every morning</i>
<i>and face what you've done?</i>
<i>Oh, fuck--</i>


01:07:40.323 --> 01:07:43.458
No, you fucking did this,
you son of a bitch.
You killed him.


01:07:43.460 --> 01:07:45.660
Hello.
<i>[ Man ]</i>
<i>911. What's your emergency?</i>


01:07:45.662 --> 01:07:46.928
Hello? I need help, okay?


01:07:46.930 --> 01:07:49.297
There's this guy.
He's trying to kill our friends.


01:07:49.299 --> 01:07:51.199
<i>Please hold.</i>
<i>He's fucking</i>
<i>killing our friends!</i>


01:07:51.201 --> 01:07:54.369
I got another choice
for you to make, Jordan.


01:07:54.371 --> 01:07:55.470
This is gonna be
a tough one.


01:07:55.472 --> 01:07:59.574
But I'm gonna give you
one last chance
to set things right.


01:07:59.576 --> 01:08:01.643
I want <i>you,</i> Jordan.


01:08:01.645 --> 01:08:03.812
<i>You'll have to pay</i>
<i>for what you did,</i>


01:08:03.814 --> 01:08:05.847
<i>and I will give you</i>
<i>the opportunity.</i>


01:08:05.849 --> 01:08:09.417
There's an old junkyard
off 17 at Canyon Junction.


01:08:09.419 --> 01:08:12.320
<i>Meet me there.</i>
<i>Turn yourself over to me,</i>


01:08:12.322 --> 01:08:16.191
I'll set your girlfriend
and Austin free.


01:08:18.127 --> 01:08:18.860
[ Screams ]


01:08:18.862 --> 01:08:22.864
<i>Please, Jordan!</i>
<i>Please help me, please!</i>
<i>Come on.</i>


01:08:22.866 --> 01:08:24.199
Please.
Please.


01:08:24.201 --> 01:08:27.969
The choice
is yours, Jordan.
Don't make me wait.


01:08:27.971 --> 01:08:30.805
Hello?
<i>I get impatient</i>
<i>when I wait.</i>


01:08:30.807 --> 01:08:32.273
I don't know where we are!


01:08:32.275 --> 01:08:35.143
Come on. You gotta help us.
He's got them.
You gotta help us!


01:08:35.145 --> 01:08:39.347
<i>Sir, I can't help you if you</i>
<i>don't tell me where you are.</i>


01:08:39.349 --> 01:08:40.582
I don't know where we are!


01:08:40.584 --> 01:08:44.486
We're, like--
We're by some junkyard.
Give me the phone!


01:08:44.488 --> 01:08:46.354
Shit!


01:08:46.356 --> 01:08:47.622
Stop the car.
No.


01:08:47.624 --> 01:08:49.958
I said stop the car.
And I said no.


01:08:49.960 --> 01:08:53.294
We can't just leave
Jewel and Austin to die.


01:08:59.902 --> 01:09:02.437
You're fucking crazy!


01:09:03.405 --> 01:09:04.772
- Come on. Let's go.
- Mickey, don't.


01:09:04.774 --> 01:09:05.740
You're coming with me.
No!


01:09:05.742 --> 01:09:08.309
If we go back there,
we're all gonna die.
Do you understand?


01:09:08.311 --> 01:09:10.912
We can't leave them.
Be smart, all right?


01:09:10.914 --> 01:09:12.280
Come with me.
We'll go get help.


01:09:12.282 --> 01:09:14.582
We'll let
the police handle this.
It'll be too late.


01:09:14.584 --> 01:09:17.519
Look. You heard
what he did to Bobby,
all right?


01:09:17.521 --> 01:09:18.553
Look, it's gotten
out of control.


01:09:18.555 --> 01:09:21.222
What makes you think
he won't do the same
to you and Jordan?


01:09:21.224 --> 01:09:23.324
I know.
Then why
are you doing this?


01:09:23.326 --> 01:09:25.627
I just--
You just what? Why?


01:09:25.629 --> 01:09:29.330
I just-- I can't--
I can't just leave them.


01:09:30.799 --> 01:09:33.234
Sounds like
she made her decision.


01:09:34.970 --> 01:09:35.904
Please don't go.


01:09:35.906 --> 01:09:39.774
This is your decision.
You wanna go with him,
go with him.


01:09:44.480 --> 01:09:48.216
If anything happens to her,
I'll kill you myself.


01:09:59.461 --> 01:10:01.629
So how are we gonna
get them back?


01:10:01.631 --> 01:10:04.332
It didn't work last time.
And now you only have me.


01:10:04.334 --> 01:10:08.436
- I'm gonna do what he says.
- Give yourself up?


01:10:08.438 --> 01:10:09.637
Yes.


01:10:09.639 --> 01:10:12.774
That's crazy.
He'll kill you.


01:10:12.776 --> 01:10:14.842
Yeah, maybe.
Maybe not.


01:10:14.844 --> 01:10:19.347
Look, if it'll
save Jewel's life,
then it's worth it.


01:10:23.452 --> 01:10:25.553
Hey!


01:10:25.555 --> 01:10:27.288
Hey!


01:10:27.890 --> 01:10:29.490
Hey!


01:10:29.492 --> 01:10:31.759
[ Horn Blaring ]


01:10:38.400 --> 01:10:39.968
Fuck.


01:11:22.745 --> 01:11:25.580
[ Grunting ]


01:11:26.682 --> 01:11:29.784
[ Siren Blaring ]


01:11:41.397 --> 01:11:43.031
Oh, God, no!


01:11:44.366 --> 01:11:46.034
Jesus Christ!


01:11:46.635 --> 01:11:47.902
Dispatch, this is Williams.


01:11:47.904 --> 01:11:51.072
Officer down!
I repeat: officer down!


01:11:51.074 --> 01:11:54.108
All units respond
to Highway 17!


01:11:54.110 --> 01:11:56.311
Mile marker--


01:11:56.712 --> 01:11:58.913
Mile marker 61.


01:12:09.692 --> 01:12:11.492
[ Grunts ]


01:12:12.895 --> 01:12:14.729
[ Groans ]


01:12:20.836 --> 01:12:22.503
No!


01:12:22.505 --> 01:12:24.439
Oh, no!


01:12:24.441 --> 01:12:26.040
No! Someone help me!


01:12:26.042 --> 01:12:27.675
No, God! Please no!


01:12:27.677 --> 01:12:31.012
Listen.
Mister, I'm sor--
I'm sorry, sir.


01:12:31.014 --> 01:12:33.448
So-- So so-sorry!


01:12:33.450 --> 01:12:35.149
[ Whimpers ]
Please!


01:12:35.151 --> 01:12:37.952
[ Grunting, Panting ]


01:12:38.887 --> 01:12:42.724
You shouldn't
have jacked me up
with the cops, Mickey.


01:12:43.459 --> 01:12:46.761
[ Flesh Squishes ]
[ Screaming ]


01:12:50.999 --> 01:12:53.034
You got ahead
of yourself.


01:12:53.036 --> 01:12:55.603
[ Skull Cracking ]


01:12:58.440 --> 01:13:00.375
That makes me mad.


01:13:01.610 --> 01:13:03.644
[ Screaming Stops ]


01:14:07.109 --> 01:14:10.445
<i>[ Police Radio Chatter ]</i>


01:14:12.948 --> 01:14:15.216
Powell just reported
he found another body.


01:14:15.218 --> 01:14:17.251
What?
Well, half a body.


01:14:17.253 --> 01:14:20.254
Female found on the side
of the road near the bridge.


01:14:20.256 --> 01:14:22.457
[ Sighs ]


01:14:25.027 --> 01:14:26.861
All right.


01:14:27.863 --> 01:14:31.098
All right.
Everyone!


01:14:31.100 --> 01:14:33.501
Over here, now!


01:14:38.841 --> 01:14:40.141
All right, listen up.


01:14:40.143 --> 01:14:42.810
Another body
has been found.


01:14:42.812 --> 01:14:44.011
I want
roadblocks on 17...


01:14:44.013 --> 01:14:49.250
and on every turnoff
to an access road
for the next 100 miles.


01:14:49.252 --> 01:14:51.118
Nobody gets through.


01:14:51.120 --> 01:14:56.157
Every vehicle gets
stopped and inspected.
Look for damage.


01:14:56.159 --> 01:14:59.093
Somebody had
to have hit Jenkins.


01:15:00.996 --> 01:15:05.666
There's a killer...
on the road.


01:15:07.002 --> 01:15:09.670
And I want him.


01:15:43.372 --> 01:15:45.740
Okay, you take the car.
You find a house.


01:15:45.742 --> 01:15:47.241
You find a gas station--
whatever it takes.


01:15:47.243 --> 01:15:50.945
And you go
to the police for help.
No, I can't leave you here.


01:15:50.947 --> 01:15:53.848
There's nothing you can do
to help me here.


01:15:54.716 --> 01:15:56.284
He's gonna kill you.
Yeah.


01:15:56.286 --> 01:15:57.919
Yeah, he's probably
gonna damn well try.


01:15:57.921 --> 01:16:01.322
Okay, but hopefully
Mickey's got the police
on the way by now.


01:16:01.324 --> 01:16:03.691
Do you think
Mickey's okay?


01:16:03.693 --> 01:16:06.394
Yeah, Mickey's a tough nut.
He's fine.


01:16:06.396 --> 01:16:08.329
But if he doesn't
have the police
on the way here,


01:16:08.331 --> 01:16:11.265
then you're
our only chance
for survival right now, okay?


01:16:11.267 --> 01:16:13.834
You.
You see this place?
It's huge.


01:16:13.836 --> 01:16:16.103
Okay, I'm gonna go in there.
I'm gonna get Austin.


01:16:16.105 --> 01:16:17.238
I'm gonna get Jewel.
We're gonna hide.


01:16:17.240 --> 01:16:21.709
And we're gonna hold up
until either you
or Mickey come back.


01:16:21.711 --> 01:16:23.210
All right.


01:16:23.212 --> 01:16:24.278
Okay.


01:16:24.280 --> 01:16:26.113
All right.


01:16:30.118 --> 01:16:33.621
[ Engine Revving ]


01:16:42.064 --> 01:16:45.933
[ Revving Fading ]


01:17:22.838 --> 01:17:24.705
Rusty, I'm here.


01:17:33.882 --> 01:17:36.851
Hey, Rusty, I'm here.


01:18:07.816 --> 01:18:09.684
Rusty, I'm here.


01:18:13.321 --> 01:18:14.855
Rusty!


01:18:14.857 --> 01:18:17.758
I said I'm here!


01:18:37.746 --> 01:18:39.413
Hey, Rusty!


01:18:39.415 --> 01:18:42.216
Come out and get me!


01:18:44.019 --> 01:18:45.986
[ Lug Wrench Taps ]


01:19:00.368 --> 01:19:03.137
[ Jewel ]
Help me!


01:19:03.139 --> 01:19:05.139
[ Screams ]


01:19:07.075 --> 01:19:10.311
Please, no! No!


01:19:26.394 --> 01:19:29.163
You know, I really like
your girlfriend.


01:19:29.165 --> 01:19:32.867
You set Jewel
and Austin free.
Then I'll surrender to you.


01:19:32.869 --> 01:19:34.068
Oh, I don't think so.


01:19:34.070 --> 01:19:37.338
We've grown so close
in the last few hours.


01:19:37.340 --> 01:19:39.240
We had a deal.
So close.


01:19:39.242 --> 01:19:42.042
I think I've got
a crush on her.


01:19:42.044 --> 01:19:43.511
[ Whimpering ]
Jewel!


01:19:43.513 --> 01:19:45.846
No!
Jewel,
I'm right here, baby!


01:19:45.848 --> 01:19:48.182
You let her go,
you son of a bitch!


01:19:50.152 --> 01:19:51.452
Maybe.


01:19:52.587 --> 01:19:55.322
What the fuck
do you mean, maybe?


01:19:55.891 --> 01:19:59.393
- I'm talking to you!
- Maybe not.


01:19:59.395 --> 01:20:01.128
Come and get her, boy.


01:20:01.130 --> 01:20:04.265
- [ Jewel ]
No!
- [ Yelling ]


01:20:06.568 --> 01:20:09.503
Learned that
from a hockey ninja.


01:20:23.985 --> 01:20:25.953
Help me!


01:20:27.689 --> 01:20:31.458
Is that the best
you've got, kid?


01:20:32.627 --> 01:20:35.162
You're gonna have
to do better than that.


01:20:35.164 --> 01:20:37.965
Fuck you.
Fuck you.


01:20:39.100 --> 01:20:41.302
[ Yells ]


01:20:44.406 --> 01:20:47.241
Oh, God!
[ Yells ]


01:20:48.310 --> 01:20:51.946
[ Bone Cracking ]
[ Chuckling ]


01:21:06.962 --> 01:21:09.163
Now don't you
go running off.


01:21:09.165 --> 01:21:13.000
[ Jewel Screaming ]


01:21:18.707 --> 01:21:20.908
[ Jewel ]
Help me!


01:21:30.485 --> 01:21:34.355
- Oh, my God!
- Jewel-- She's in the crusher.
Shut it off!


01:21:34.357 --> 01:21:36.123
How?
Turn the switch!


01:21:36.125 --> 01:21:38.125
Quickly!
Shut it off!


01:21:39.361 --> 01:21:41.128
Help me up.


01:21:41.130 --> 01:21:43.430
Give me that.
Please, help!


01:21:43.432 --> 01:21:48.102
Jewel! Jewel!
I'm coming, baby!


01:21:53.174 --> 01:21:55.242
Jewel!
Jewel!


01:21:55.510 --> 01:21:59.146
Oh. What the hell? No.


01:21:59.148 --> 01:22:01.315
Oh, shit.


01:22:02.384 --> 01:22:04.151
Oh, sh--


01:22:04.519 --> 01:22:07.554
<i>[ Recording: Saw Whirring ]</i>


01:22:09.157 --> 01:22:10.791
Shit.


01:22:10.793 --> 01:22:15.329
<i>Oh, my God! Oh, my God!</i>
<i>No! No! No!</i>


01:22:15.331 --> 01:22:18.065
<i>No! Oh, God! No!</i>


01:22:18.067 --> 01:22:20.534
<i>Please! No! Please!</i>


01:22:20.536 --> 01:22:24.171
<i>Oh, God, no!</i>


01:22:24.173 --> 01:22:25.472
<i>[ Sobbing ]</i>


01:22:25.474 --> 01:22:31.478
<i>Oh, please! Oh, God!</i>
<i>Please God! No!</i>


01:22:31.480 --> 01:22:34.181
Oh, God!


01:22:34.183 --> 01:22:37.952
Oh, God. Please.
[ Sobbing ]


01:22:43.024 --> 01:22:46.293
[ Screams ]
No! No! Please!


01:22:50.198 --> 01:22:52.533
Oh, my God! No!


01:22:52.535 --> 01:22:54.368
No! No! Please!


01:22:54.370 --> 01:22:57.037
Oh, God!
Help me, God!


01:23:03.478 --> 01:23:05.346
No, please!


01:23:08.350 --> 01:23:10.117
No! No!


01:23:11.052 --> 01:23:12.286
No!


01:23:13.254 --> 01:23:15.723
Oh, God!
Oh, God!


01:23:18.093 --> 01:23:19.293
Oh, God!


01:23:19.728 --> 01:23:23.097
Please, don't!
Don't! No! No!


01:23:23.099 --> 01:23:24.598
No, no, no! No!


01:23:24.600 --> 01:23:28.235
No! Please!
[ Screams ]


01:23:28.237 --> 01:23:32.539
No, no, no!
[ Screams ]


01:23:36.044 --> 01:23:42.116
Well, you're halfway
to the hospital now, Jewel.
[ Chuckling ]


01:23:51.593 --> 01:23:56.030
I'll fucking kill him.
I'm gonna fucking kill him!


01:23:57.198 --> 01:23:58.999
[ Yells ]


01:24:11.846 --> 01:24:14.515
- Where is he?
- He's gone.


01:24:14.849 --> 01:24:16.817
His truck's gone.
Come on.


01:24:16.819 --> 01:24:19.353
We've gotta find him!


01:24:20.088 --> 01:24:22.623
[ Engine Cranking ]


01:24:25.193 --> 01:24:27.728
[ Horn Blaring ]


01:24:31.599 --> 01:24:32.800
My leg!


01:24:38.740 --> 01:24:41.442
Come on!
We gotta get
out of here!


01:24:43.311 --> 01:24:45.379
We gotta get out.


01:24:47.215 --> 01:24:49.183
We gotta get out.


01:24:49.451 --> 01:24:51.485
Oh, my God.
I'm stuck!


01:24:51.487 --> 01:24:52.586
What?
My leg is stuck!


01:24:52.588 --> 01:24:55.189
- What do you mean?
- [ Shrieks ]


01:24:55.191 --> 01:24:57.224
Get it out!


01:24:59.360 --> 01:25:02.296
I can't
get it either.
[ Shrieks ]


01:25:13.608 --> 01:25:15.642
Come on, come on!


01:25:17.679 --> 01:25:20.681
That's it. That's it.
All right. Yes!


01:25:22.350 --> 01:25:23.383
All right, come on.


01:25:23.385 --> 01:25:25.552
All right.
Here we go.


01:25:43.605 --> 01:25:46.173
- Come on.
- Hurry.


01:25:49.477 --> 01:25:51.612
No, no, no.
Go back. Back.


01:25:56.651 --> 01:25:58.519
Yeah, yeah, yeah!


01:25:59.254 --> 01:26:00.821
[ Grunts ]


01:26:01.489 --> 01:26:02.856
Yes!


01:26:04.392 --> 01:26:07.427
You like that, Rusty? Huh?


01:26:19.374 --> 01:26:21.575
Here we go.


01:26:26.948 --> 01:26:28.615
[ Grunting ]


01:26:34.522 --> 01:26:37.891
You like that?
How about you go in the crusher?


01:26:46.968 --> 01:26:48.769
Yeah!


01:26:54.642 --> 01:26:56.677
Come on.


01:26:57.612 --> 01:26:59.746
Okay, that's it.


01:27:07.021 --> 01:27:10.557
Yeah! Boom!
[ Laughs ]


01:27:33.881 --> 01:27:37.718
[ Grunting ]


01:27:50.632 --> 01:27:53.267
[ Growls ]


01:28:03.578 --> 01:28:06.313
Alisa!
<i>[ Thunderclap ]</i>


01:28:06.648 --> 01:28:10.317
Alisa,
are you all right?
Come on. I got you.


01:28:18.593 --> 01:28:20.427
He's dead.


01:28:23.998 --> 01:28:26.466
Let's get out of here.


01:28:27.635 --> 01:28:29.436
Yeah.


01:28:42.450 --> 01:28:46.353
[ Sirens Blaring ]


01:29:07.175 --> 01:29:09.710
He said his name
was Rusty Nail.


01:29:09.911 --> 01:29:13.547
- A C.B. handle?
- Yeah, something like that.


01:29:13.848 --> 01:29:19.052
Any idea why he would want
to hurt you and your friends?


01:29:19.054 --> 01:29:21.722
Because he was
a psychopath.


01:29:21.724 --> 01:29:23.523
Yeah, okay.


01:29:23.525 --> 01:29:25.859
The M.E. is ready
for them now.


01:29:26.761 --> 01:29:27.160
Got it.


01:29:27.162 --> 01:29:32.566
Detective Assael is going
to take the two of you
down to the coroner's office.


01:29:32.568 --> 01:29:37.037
We need you...
to identify a body.


01:29:38.973 --> 01:29:40.807
Who is it?


01:29:42.176 --> 01:29:45.178
Well,
we can't say for sure,


01:29:45.180 --> 01:29:47.781
but we believe
it's a Mr. Cole.


01:29:51.753 --> 01:29:53.720
Mickey.


01:29:53.722 --> 01:29:55.655
I'm sorry.


01:29:58.793 --> 01:30:00.761
[ Sobs ]


01:30:03.164 --> 01:30:05.399
They're ready to go.


01:30:25.520 --> 01:30:27.854
Nobody could
survive this.


01:30:29.924 --> 01:30:32.392
Well, open her up.


01:30:34.095 --> 01:30:36.129
I want to see the body.


01:30:37.665 --> 01:30:40.767
[ Man ]
Okay, coming up.
Back off!


01:30:41.502 --> 01:30:43.403
Okay. We'll wait.


01:31:11.566 --> 01:31:13.834
He's still out there.


01:31:51.973 --> 01:31:54.307
Hey.
Thanks for stopping.


01:31:54.309 --> 01:31:57.244
You want a lift, buddy?
Yes, sir.


01:31:57.246 --> 01:31:59.079
Climb on in.


01:32:09.257 --> 01:32:11.191
What's your name?


01:32:12.159 --> 01:32:13.860
Rusty.


01:32:13.862 --> 01:32:15.161
Rusty Nail.


01:32:15.163 --> 01:32:18.131
Closed-Captioned by
Captions, Inc., Burbank, CA


